GitHub Actions Marketplace

Today I explored how the Actions Marketplace helps reuse automation instead of building everything from scratch.

🔹 Using Public Actions
Public actions provide:
Prebuilt automation
Common CI/CD tasks
Faster workflow setup
They reduce pipeline complexity.

🔹 Action Versions
Actions are referenced using versions:
Version tags
Release numbers
Commit SHAs
Pinning versions improves stability.

🔹 Trusted Actions
Use verified publishers
Review action source code
Avoid untrusted repositories
Security starts with trusted actions.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Reuse saves time.
 Versions ensure stability.
 Trust protects pipelines.
